Hi,
	I have finished a port of the zd1211 driver to the Devicescape 802.11 stac=
k.=20
Due to the size of the patch, the patch that copies the zd1211 directory to=
=20
the d80211 directory has been omitted, but can be found at my git repo.=20
(git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/mwu/d80211-drivers.git up) T=
he=20
two other patches relevant to porting the driver are bzip2ed and attached d=
ue=20
to size concerns.

This port works fairly well in STA mode, with adhoc and monitor modes to co=
me=20
in the future. I tried to minimize changes to the structure of the driver a=
nd=20
code whenever possible to make it easier to port patches from the softmac=20
based zd1211 driver to this driver. However:

	- The original driver does not seem to check if a frame has been successfu=
lly=20
TXed (as in RXed an ACK), so the port does not properly report to the stack=
=20
whether or not a TX succeeded.
	-Because d80211 does not have complete regulatory domains support yet, the=
=20
associated code was trimmed to the bare minimum of reading the region code.=
=20
It should be a trivial patch to add regulatory domains support once the=20
infrastructure is in place in d80211.
	- d80211 doesn't tell us the size of the next fragment, so that part of th=
e=20
hardware TX header isn't set anymore. This might be fixed in the future.
	- The LED link status isn't too reliable - I haven't found a way to reliab=
ly=20
tell if the upper layer thinks it is associated, and I don't know how to us=
e=20
the LED api. Not too worried about this issue though.

I will push this to wireless-dev soon if there are no major problems.

Thanks,
=2DMichael Wu

